{title: 487 - In the Garden}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #487 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 487}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]I come to the garden alone, [Eb7]While the dew is still on the roses;
[Ab]And the voice I hear, falling on my ear, The Son of God discloses.
[Ab]And He walks with me, And [Db/Ab]He talks with me, And He [Ab]tells me I am His own;
[Ab]And the joy we share [Gdim]as we tarrythere, None other [Eb]has ever known.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Ab]And He walks with me, and He talks with me,
[Ab]And He tells me I am His own;
[Ab]And the joy we [Gdim]share as we [Eb/Bb]tarry there,
[Cm]None other has ever known.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]He speaks, and the [Eb7]sound of His voice
[Ab]Is so sweet the birds hush their singing,
[Ab]And the melody [Db/Ab]that He [Ab]gave to me
[Ab]Within [Gdim]my heart is [Eb]ringing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]I'd stay in the [Eb7]garden with Him
[Ab]Though the night around me be falling,
[Ab]But He bids me [Db/Ab]go; through the [Ab]voice of woe,
[Ab]His voice [Gdim]to me is [Eb]calling.
{end_of_verse}
